# Vercel builds the React frontend only. The retrieval/audit backend cannot run
# as a serverless function and must not be bundled into one.
#
# Why: requirements.txt pulls torch, faiss-cpu, lightgbm, transformers, scipy
# and sklearn. On Vercel's Linux runners that installed to 5,675 MB against a
# 500 MB function limit. Trimming dependencies would not rescue it either — the
# engine loads a 470 MB embedding model, builds an index over 6,383 standards
# in ~50s, and then serves from that index in memory. A serverless function has
# no memory between invocations, so every cold start would pay the full build.
#
# The backend belongs on a container host; backend/Dockerfile builds it with
# the model and embeddings baked in. (Long term, government deployment requires
# MeitY-empanelled hosting anyway, so Vercel was always a demo stopgap here.)

backend/
data_pipeline/
data/
services/
standards-retrieval/
app/
api/
tests/
scripts/
scratch/
ingest.py
requirements.txt
